1
00:00:02,513 --> 00:00:06,601
[Subtitles by danielsangeo]

2
00:00:07,219 --> 00:00:11,171
[metal banging]
Man, I'm a VIP, I don't have to take this.

3
00:00:11,171 --> 00:00:12,234
[tentacles moan]

4
00:00:12,234 --> 00:00:13,416
[tentacles moan]
Hey, your buddy's dead,

5
00:00:13,416 --> 00:00:14,293
[tentacles moan]
but I didn't do it,

6
00:00:14,293 --> 00:00:15,361
[tentacles moan]
so that means you're a witness

7
00:00:15,361 --> 00:00:16,903
[tentacles moan]
if somebody asks about it later.

8
00:00:16,903 --> 00:00:18,018
[metal banging]

9
00:00:18,018 --> 00:00:19,744
[metal banging]
That guard's just standing there.

10
00:00:19,744 --> 00:00:21,358
[tentacles moan]
I don't know why.

11
00:00:21,358 --> 00:00:22,091
[tentacles moan]

12
00:00:22,091 --> 00:00:23,254
[metal banging]
Maybe it's his job to guard

13
00:00:23,254 --> 00:00:26,114
the explosives from being eaten by aliens.

14
00:00:26,114 --> 00:00:29,163
All things considered, I think we
should let the aliens eat the explosives

15
00:00:29,163 --> 00:00:30,129
[tentacles moan]
if they want to.

16
00:00:30,129 --> 00:00:30,972
[tentacles moan]

17
00:00:30,972 --> 00:00:32,564
[tentacles moan]
Hah! I flanked you.

18
00:00:32,564 --> 00:00:33,366
[tentacles moan]

19
00:00:33,366 --> 00:00:35,165
[tentacles moan]
Well, I'm going to assume that because this

20
00:00:35,165 --> 00:00:36,439
[tentacles moan]
is the most dangerous-looking thing

21
00:00:36,439 --> 00:00:37,767
[tentacles moan]
I've seen in my life,

22
00:00:37,767 --> 00:00:39,411
I'm going the right way.

23
00:00:39,411 --> 00:00:41,667
[metal banging]
God! Look at how big this thing is!

24
00:00:42,143 --> 00:00:44,204
This is completely unacceptable.

25
00:00:44,204 --> 00:00:45,816
We don't have room for this.

26
00:00:45,816 --> 00:00:46,866
[tentacles moan]
That thing's already

27
00:00:46,866 --> 00:00:48,209
[metal banging]
half-buried in the floor.

28
00:00:48,209 --> 00:00:49,168
[tentacles moan]

29
00:00:49,168 --> 00:00:51,033
[metal banging]
That's right. I bang, you bang,

30
00:00:51,033 --> 00:00:52,303
[metal banging]
we all bang together.

31
00:00:52,303 --> 00:00:53,785
[tentacles moan]

32
00:00:53,785 --> 00:00:55,646
[tentacles moan]
What was that Nietzsche said?

33
00:00:55,646 --> 00:00:56,750
[tentacles moan]
"He who fights drummers

34
00:00:56,750 --> 00:00:57,648
[tentacles moan]
"should see to it that

35
00:00:57,648 --> 00:00:58,741
[tentacles moan]
"in the process he does not

36
00:00:58,741 --> 00:01:00,101
[metal banging]
"become a drummer?"

37
00:01:00,101 --> 00:01:01,757
[tentacles moan]
Or was it "monsters"?

38
00:01:01,757 --> 00:01:03,554
[tentacles moan]
I don't know. Same thing, really.

39
00:01:03,554 --> 00:01:06,260
[tentacles moan]

40
00:01:06,260 --> 00:01:08,342
[tentacles moan]
No, it had to be "drummers".

41
00:01:08,342 --> 00:01:11,803
That's a monster and there's no way
I'm going to end up look like that thing.

42
00:01:11,803 --> 00:01:14,166
I wonder if Nietzsche was in a band.

43
00:01:14,166 --> 00:01:17,446
I bet he was. I should look him
up when I get out of here.

44
00:01:17,446 --> 00:01:19,876
I bet the songs have pretty deep lyrics.

45
00:01:19,876 --> 00:01:21,375
[explosion]
Ho!

46
00:01:22,346 --> 00:01:24,086
Huh, twice in a row.

47
00:01:24,086 --> 00:01:26,866
I feel like I should be learning
something from this.

48
00:01:26,866 --> 00:01:29,500
And, of course, the catwalk
folds like cardboard,

49
00:01:29,500 --> 00:01:32,064
but the frigging pipes are fine.

50
00:01:32,064 --> 00:01:39,700
[whistling "The Man on the Flying Trapeze"]

51
00:01:39,700 --> 00:01:40,701
I'm awesome.

52
00:01:42,142 --> 00:01:44,203
Hey, there's that other ledge!

53
00:01:44,203 --> 00:01:47,244
If I had a hang glider, I could've
just swooped down here.

54
00:01:47,244 --> 00:01:48,849
And that ledge, too!

55
00:01:48,849 --> 00:01:50,670
That would be sick!

56
00:01:50,670 --> 00:01:51,342
[growls]

57
00:01:51,342 --> 00:01:53,601
This place frustrates me to no end.

58
00:01:54,089 --> 00:01:56,370
I guess the light at the end of
the tunnel here is that it should be

59
00:01:56,370 --> 00:01:58,968
pretty easy for me to get a new job now.

60
00:01:58,968 --> 00:02:02,351
Seriously, the military is going to get
a hard-on once they realize they have

61
00:02:02,351 --> 00:02:05,269
honest-to-God monsters that big to attack.

62
00:02:05,269 --> 00:02:08,402
The US is certain to dump
boatloads into defense spending

63
00:02:08,402 --> 00:02:10,261
on top of what we already have.

64
00:02:10,261 --> 00:02:13,529
There's going to be a lot of trickling
down to research and development.

65
00:02:13,529 --> 00:02:16,261
Hell, I could be driving a
Porsche before the year is out.

66
00:02:16,821 --> 00:02:17,619
[lock buzzes]

67
00:02:17,619 --> 00:02:18,801
Piece of crap.

68
00:02:19,640 --> 00:02:22,134
I guess the big danger to such
massive defense spending

69
00:02:22,134 --> 00:02:26,266
is that we might end up as a military
city-state perpetually at war with aliens.

70
00:02:26,266 --> 00:02:28,071
[zombies grunt]
Like "Starship Troopers".

71
00:02:28,071 --> 00:02:29,047
[zombies grunt]
What's that noise?

72
00:02:29,047 --> 00:02:30,142
[zombies grunt]

73
00:02:30,142 --> 00:02:31,693
[zombies grunt]
Oh, someone thinks they're smarter

74
00:02:31,693 --> 00:02:32,661
[zombies grunt]
than me, huh?

75
00:02:32,661 --> 00:02:33,310
[zombies grunt]

76
00:02:33,310 --> 00:02:34,955
[zombies grunt]
I don't need to dignify this.

77
00:02:34,955 --> 00:02:35,868
[zombies grunt]

78
00:02:36,703 --> 00:02:38,367
YOU DON'T EVEN HAVE A DEGREE!

79
00:02:39,956 --> 00:02:42,849
Actually, your host bodies have
degrees around here,

80
00:02:42,849 --> 00:02:44,742
but you're just latching on to that.

81
00:02:44,742 --> 00:02:47,515
That's even worse than one of
those online degrees.

82
00:02:47,515 --> 00:02:49,811
You're a parasite in every way.

83
00:02:49,811 --> 00:02:51,483
Oh. Safety bars.

84
00:02:51,483 --> 00:02:54,767
Knowing this place, that means
somebody must've fallen in at one point.

85
00:02:55,556 --> 00:02:59,801
And we put up cardboard tubes
wrapped in tin foil apparently.

86
00:03:00,870 --> 00:03:03,839
This is so cool, it's just like
Super Mario.

87
00:03:03,839 --> 00:03:08,356
[whistles "Super Mario Bros." theme]

88
00:03:08,356 --> 00:03:09,711
I like Mario.

89
00:03:09,711 --> 00:03:13,008
It's a game that glorifies the
fat blue-collar worker.

90
00:03:13,008 --> 00:03:17,033
People will have to learn to appreciate
their station in life once I rise to power.

91
00:03:17,521 --> 00:03:29,962
[whistles underground theme from "Super Mario"]

92
00:03:29,962 --> 00:03:31,836
What is this place?

93
00:03:31,836 --> 00:03:34,236
Oh, I hate forks like this!

94
00:03:34,236 --> 00:03:38,488
Because I know whichever path I take,
it's going to change my life forever.

95
00:03:38,488 --> 00:03:41,033
Okay, did I pick the right one?

96
00:03:42,568 --> 00:03:43,701
I did NOT.

97
00:03:44,499 --> 00:03:45,434
Shit.

98
00:03:46,434 --> 00:03:49,753
Now I'm always going to be
10-seconds behind in life.

99
00:03:49,753 --> 00:03:52,084
That means I may miss
meeting my future wife

100
00:03:52,084 --> 00:03:54,280
or escaping an assassin's bullet.

101
00:03:54,280 --> 00:03:58,061
I'll be without a throne or heir
all because of this stupid dungeon.

102
00:03:58,061 --> 00:03:59,479
This is so unfair!

103
00:03:59,479 --> 00:04:01,931
I AM DESTINED FOR GREATNESS!

104
00:04:01,931 --> 00:04:03,467
I'll show everyone...

105
00:04:04,481 --> 00:04:09,699
Y'know, it would make this whole day almost
worth it if I found buried treasure here?

106
00:04:09,699 --> 00:04:11,701
I mean, this is the place for it to be.

107
00:04:12,558 --> 00:04:14,000
Either that, or some bodies.

108
00:04:14,674 --> 00:04:17,163
Oh, cool, I didn't go in circles again.

109
00:04:17,163 --> 00:04:19,787
Okay, going to have to hook my arm here...

110
00:04:20,294 --> 00:04:21,400
There we go.

111
00:04:23,044 --> 00:04:23,467
Yah.

112
00:04:24,155 --> 00:04:27,167
Whoa-whoa-whoa! I'm supposed to
be the stalker, not you!

113
00:04:27,167 --> 00:04:28,467
Get off my turf!

114
00:04:29,483 --> 00:04:30,549
Perfect.

115
00:04:30,549 --> 00:04:31,315
I mean, what the hell?

116
00:04:31,315 --> 00:04:34,407
You sneak out of the manhole and
somebody's already waiting for you.

117
00:04:34,407 --> 00:04:35,443
Eh, I'm good.

118
00:04:35,443 --> 00:04:38,029
I will say, with as many grenades
lying around as I've seen,

119
00:04:38,029 --> 00:04:41,574
I am a little surprised we haven't
had a bigger accident before today.

120
00:04:41,574 --> 00:04:42,534
Oh, come on.

121
00:04:45,682 --> 00:04:48,844
Man, when I get a mansion, this
is exactly what it'll be like.

122
00:04:48,844 --> 00:04:50,379
People will knock on the door,

123
00:04:50,379 --> 00:04:52,146
the butler will answer the door,

124
00:04:52,146 --> 00:04:53,958
blow them away with a shotgun,

125
00:04:53,958 --> 00:04:55,347
then close the door.

126
00:04:55,347 --> 00:04:57,455
And I guess I'll need a couple
people to move the bodies

127
00:04:57,455 --> 00:04:59,382
so they don't rot on the property.

128
00:04:59,382 --> 00:05:02,434
I can't realistically expect the
butler to--where am I?

129
00:05:03,145 --> 00:05:06,774
I can't expect the butler to do
that by himself without dragging them,

130
00:05:06,774 --> 00:05:08,930
and that would mark up the floors.

131
00:05:08,930 --> 00:05:11,901
And if it was a really fat guy,
they might need a hand-trolley.

132
00:05:12,769 --> 00:05:15,101
Yeah, I don't know, there's a
lot of planning involved,

133
00:05:15,101 --> 00:05:17,534
I'll just have to take this
one step at a time.

134
00:05:18,577 --> 00:05:23,556
This room reminds me of that place in Star
Wars where Darth Vader cuts off Luke's hand.

135
00:05:23,556 --> 00:05:25,965
Man, I wish lightsabers were real.

136
00:05:25,965 --> 00:05:28,310
I don't see why you need "the Force"

137
00:05:28,310 --> 00:05:31,420
if you have an energy sword that
can cut through anything.

138
00:05:31,420 --> 00:05:33,667
All you need then is a list of demands.

139
00:05:34,098 --> 00:05:36,863
Damn, I was hoping for a
maintenance shaft here.

140
00:05:36,863 --> 00:05:37,648
What's this do?

141
00:05:37,648 --> 00:05:38,906
[electricity humming]

142
00:05:38,906 --> 00:05:39,500
Nothing?

143
00:05:40,182 --> 00:05:41,672
There's really no excuse for hav--

144
00:05:41,672 --> 00:05:42,580
[WHOOSH]
Urgh...

145
00:05:42,580 --> 00:05:43,300
OW!

146
00:05:44,235 --> 00:05:47,033
JESUS CHRIST! THAT COULD'VE
TAKEN MY HEAD OFF!

147
00:05:47,573 --> 00:05:49,500
WHO THE FUCK DESIGNED THIS?!

148
00:05:49,929 --> 00:05:52,543
How are you supposed to turn
that on without dying?

149
00:05:52,543 --> 00:05:54,367
How are you even supposed to turn it off?

150
00:05:54,879 --> 00:05:56,534
Is that what all these
grenades are for?

151
00:05:57,090 --> 00:06:00,041
I guess I don't have anyone
to blame but myself.

152
00:06:00,041 --> 00:06:04,051
You go around pushing enough buttons
on heavy machinery and you end up in trouble.

153
00:06:04,051 --> 00:06:06,601
At least there were no witnesses this time.

154
00:06:06,601 --> 00:06:07,915
[wind howls]
I mean this is nothing

155
00:06:07,915 --> 00:06:10,404
[wind howls]
compared to wood shop back in high school.

156
00:06:10,404 --> 00:06:12,436
[wind howls]
I almost got expelled over that.

157
00:06:12,436 --> 00:06:13,652
[wind howls]
[lock buzzes]

158
00:06:13,652 --> 00:06:14,198
[wind howls]
What?

159
00:06:14,198 --> 00:06:15,180
[wind howls]

160
00:06:15,180 --> 00:06:16,794
[wind howls]
ARE YOU KIDDING ME?!

161
00:06:16,794 --> 00:06:18,467
[wind howls]
YOU CAN'T OPEN THIS FROM THE INSIDE

162
00:06:18,467 --> 00:06:20,690
[wind howls]
AND IT AUTOMATICALLY SHUTS?!

163
00:06:20,690 --> 00:06:22,406
[wind howls]
[growls]

164
00:06:22,406 --> 00:06:23,805
[wind howls]
I think there needs to be a sign

165
00:06:23,805 --> 00:06:24,927
[wind howls]
on the outside that says

166
00:06:24,927 --> 00:06:26,176
[wind howls]
"Please prop the door or else

167
00:06:26,176 --> 00:06:27,732
[wind howls]
"you'll die a slow death."

168
00:06:27,732 --> 00:06:31,084
[wind howls]

169
00:06:31,084 --> 00:06:32,975
[wind howls]
I wonder if the aliens are edible.

170
00:06:32,975 --> 00:06:37,500
[wind howls]

